**Bus factor: 2 by ownership, but 1 if you count only people who are still active.** These figures come from surviving-lines at 62628c0. The formatting commit 62628c0 is set aside, and its lines go back to the earlier authors.

**Whole repository** (1,662 non-blank lines, 1,985 counting blank lines, 315 commits)

| Author | Non-blank lines | Counting blank lines | Commits |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 605 (36.4%) | 762 (38.4%) | 93 (29.5%) |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 551 (33.2%) | 629 (31.7%) | 143 (45.4%) |

- **Ownership:** these two hold more than 50% of the lines, so the bus factor is 2. Reaching 80% takes 5 authors.
- **Activity:** only 9 of 44 people have committed in the last 365 days, and they hold 51.7% of the lines. Counting only those people, the bus factor is 1, and that person is **Troy Goode**.
- **Wilson:** he is the largest contributor by commits, but he has no commit in that window. His 33.2% of the lines is effectively unmaintained.
- **Same person, two addresses:** Troy Goode also appears under `troy@laptop.example`. If that is the same person, his share rises to 649 lines (39.0%). This is a guess from names and addresses, and I haven't applied it.

**Where it depends on a single person**

- **`lib/`** (214 lines, 12.9% of the code): Troy Goode holds 61.7%. This is the core library code, so it is the most important dependency.
- **`test/`** (820 lines, 49.3%): Troy Goode holds 47.3%. `test/vary.js` is a single-owner file (Troy Goode, 32 lines).
- **`.github/`** (305 lines, 18.4%): Wilson holds 30.2%. Two workflows have one author each:
  - `scorecard.yml`: Íñigo Marquínez Prado, 61 lines. The name is garbled in the tool output.
  - `codeql.yml`: Sebastian Beltran, 53 lines.
- **Root files** (323 lines, 19.4%): Wilson holds 29.4%.

**Orphaned files** (top owner inactive, and nobody active holds 20% or more): 6 of 18 files, 7.8% of the lines. The largest are:
- `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml` (Marquínez Prado, 61 lines)
- `HISTORY.md` (Wilson, 41 lines)
- `LICENSE` (Wilson, 18 lines)

**Caveats**
- 48.3% of the lines belong to people with no commit in the last 365 days. The largest holders are Wilson (33.2%) and Marquínez Prado (4.8%).
- The activity window is measured as of 2026-04-12, not today (2026-10-24). Anyone whose last commit fell between those dates may now count as inactive.
- `dependabot[bot]` (10 lines, 11 commits) is left out of every number.
- The scorecard and CodeQL workflows were committed by GitHub, but the lines are credited to their real authors.

**Recommendation:** have a second person review and touch `lib/` and `test/` so Troy Goode is no longer the only maintainer of the core code. Also assign owners for the orphaned CI and docs files.

